{
"_doc": [
  "The IMR instance's course layer (tools/instance.json layer.course; design note docs/reviews/2026-11-25-imr-layer-round-3.md section 1.4): the references of the IMR lecture's photos. The photos themselves stay in img/ and on R2 (whether they stay in play is a separate decision).",
  "course: {genus (data.json gen): [photo record]}, the lecture's photos in data.json course order: f (the file, imr-... or imrl-...), imr: true, slide, v (its view) and the rest of the record (ar, a and pg, the Corals of the World credit traced by tools/apply_imr_sources.py, cr, ro, iv, multi, src). One genus per line.",
  "cmp: the lecture's look-alike comparison records (data.json cmp records with imr: true); the sources' own cmp records stay in data.json.",
  "data.json carries a copy where it always had them. tools/datajson.py is the one writer of both: dump() writes the course and the lecture's cmp records it is given to this file and data.json gets the same, load() lays this file on what it reads, and python3 tools/datajson.py (and --check) give data.json as this file says. Edit the records with the tools that write data.json (tools/apply_*.py), or by hand here, then run python3 tools/datajson.py. Layout: tools/instance.py layer_dumps (one genus per line)."
],
